# What the Lucy <-> swarmbuild two-way sync (swarm_twoway_sync.py) NEVER reads, copies or deletes, in either direction.
# Syntax (gitignore-like): '/x' is anchored at the tree root, 'x/' matches directories only, '*' stays inside one path
# component, '**/x' matches at any depth, '!x' re-includes. The last matching rule wins.
# Built into the tool regardless of this file: /.git/  /.sync-trash/  /.swarm-sync/
#
# Rule of thumb: source, scripts, docs, images and config sync both ways. Anything the build produces, and anything that
# only exists on one side by design, stays out, so it can neither flow into the source tree nor be mistaken for a deletion.

## housekeeping
lost+found/
.Trash-*/
.swarm-build.lock

## only exists, or only matters, on the build side
/swarm_os_build_work/
/install-env/
/swarm_os_out/
/30-source/flutter-sdk/
/logs/

## moved to its own build partition (/mnt/lucillebuild) on 2026-10-09; never sync it back
/30-source/LucilleAssistant/

## build output and generated files: rebuilt on swarmbuild, must never flow back into the source tree
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.dart_tool/
**/.gradle/
**/__pycache__/
**/ephemeral/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.o
/30-source/frontend/build/
/30-source/lucille-core/build/
/30-source/lucille-core/build.old-from-Lucy/
/30-source/*/obj/

## untracked build products compiled into the source tree by the build (the dev server runs from ~/.local/bin, not from these)
/30-source/GamingAgent-go/gaming-agent
/30-source/LucyServer-go/lucy-server
/30-source/LucyServer-go/swarm-memory

## root-owned backups written by the grub scripts (some files unreadable by the normal user)
/grub_themes/backups/

## the ISO profile's staged copies of built programs (gitignored for the same reason); usr/lib/swarm is real source
/40-iso-profile/*/airootfs/opt/
/40-iso-profile/*/airootfs/var/cache/
/40-iso-profile/*/airootfs/usr/lib/*
!/40-iso-profile/*/airootfs/usr/lib/swarm/
/40-iso-profile/*/airootfs/usr/local/share/swarm-os/airootfs.tar

## disk images and ISOs live on Ventoy / in VMs, never in the trees
*.iso
*.sfs
*.qcow2
*.img
